

Scanner is a Java class used to read input from the keyboard (or other input sources). For DSA, you'll mostly use nextInt(), nextLong(), next(), and nextLine().

| Method             | Reads          |
| ------------------ | -------------- |
| `nextInt()`        | Integer        |
| `nextLong()`       | Long integer   |
| `nextDouble()`     | Decimal number |
| `next()`           | One word       |
| `nextLine()`       | Entire line    |
| `next().charAt(0)` | One character  |


For Array : 
Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

int n = sc.nextInt();
int[] arr = new int[n];

for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    arr[i] = sc.nextInt();
}

for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");
}

sc.close();



